From: bufadu <1352301+bufadu@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: nanopi-r3s-lts: keep vccio_sd on

dw_mmc disables vqmmc when the SD card is powered off at shutdown. The RK809
LDO is not reset by a warm reboot, so the SD I/O domain stays unpowered and
the factory eMMC SPL falls back to the eMMC system.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-nanopi-r3s-lts.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-nanopi-r3s-lts.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-nanopi-r3s-lts.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-nanopi-r3s-lts.dts
@@ -60,6 +60,16 @@
 	/delete-property/ sd-uhs-sdr50;
 };
 
+/*
+ * Linux turns vqmmc off when it powers the card down at shutdown. The RK809
+ * keeps that state across a warm reset, so the SD I/O domain is unpowered
+ * when the eMMC SPL probes the card and it fails "voltage select". Keep it on.
+ */
+&vccio_sd {
+	regulator-always-on;
+	regulator-boot-on;
+};
+
 &vp0 {
 	vp0_out_hdmi: endpoint@ROCKCHIP_VOP2_EP_HDMI0 {
 		reg = <ROCKCHIP_VOP2_EP_HDMI0>;
